19:T596,## When behaviour depends on a mode

A document behaves differently when it's a **draft**, **in moderation**, or **published**. The naive version scatters the same conditional everywhere:

```
void publish() {
    if (state == DRAFT)       state = MODERATION;
    else if (state == MODERATION) state = (isAdmin ? PUBLISHED : MODERATION);
    else if (state == PUBLISHED)  { /* nothing */ }
}
// …and the same if/else repeated in edit(), render(), …
```

Every new state means editing every method. It's fragile and unreadable.

## Make each state a class

Pull each state into its own **State** object that implements a shared interface. The **Context** (`Document`) holds a reference to its *current* State and **delegates** every request to it:

```
class Document {
    private State state = new Draft();
    void publish() { state.publish(this); }   // delegate
    void setState(State s) { this.state = s; }
}
```

Each State handles the request **its own way** and decides the **next** state by calling `document.setState(...)`. The giant conditional disappears, the logic lives where it belongs.

## State vs Strategy

Same structure (a context delegating to an interface), different intent: a **Strategy** is chosen by the client and rarely changes; **State** transitions happen *internally*, and the states often know about each other to drive the next transition. Think of it as an object-oriented **state machine**.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-behavioral","activeLesson":"state"}],["$","$L18","state",{"lesson":{"id":"state","patternId":"lld-behavioral","title":"State","kind":"pattern","difficulty":"Core","statement":"Let an object change its behaviour when its internal state changes, so it appears to switch class, by delegating to a State object instead of a wall of if/else.","companies":["Amazon","Uber","Atlassian"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"A state object per state","code":["interface State { void publish(Document d); }","class Draft      implements State { ... }","class Moderation implements State { ... }","class Published  implements State { ... }","class Document { State state; void publish(){ state.publish(this); } }"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":5,"narration":"The Document is the Context. It holds its CURRENT State and delegates every call, publish(), edit(), straight to it.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"doc","name":"Document","fields":["- state: State"],"methods":["+ publish()","+ edit()"],"x":0,"y":0.4},{"id":"state","name":"State","stereotype":"interface","methods":["+ publish(doc)","+ edit(doc)"],"x":1.6,"y":0.1,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"draft","name":"Draft","methods":["+ publish()"],"x":1,"y":1.6},{"id":"mod","name":"Moderation","methods":["+ publish()"],"x":1.95,"y":1.6},{"id":"pub","name":"Published","methods":["+ publish()"],"x":2.95,"y":1.6}],"relations":[{"id":"h","from":"doc","to":"state","kind":"aggregate","label":"current"},{"id":"d","from":"draft","to":"state","kind":"implement"},{"id":"m","from":"mod","to":"state","kind":"implement"},{"id":"p","from":"pub","to":"state","kind":"implement"}],"shownClassIds":["doc","state"],"shownRelIds":["h"],"activeIds":["doc"]},"vars":[["Document","delegates to state"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":2,"narration":"Each phase becomes a class: Draft, Moderation, Published, all implementing the State interface, each with its own behaviour.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["doc","state","draft","mod","pub"],"shownRelIds":["h","d","m","p"],"activeIds":["draft","mod","pub"]}}]},{"label":"States drive the transitions","code":["class Draft implements State {","    void publish(Document d){ d.setState(new Moderation()); }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"state","codeLine":1,"narration":"The document starts in Draft. Behaviour and the allowed transitions are whatever the Draft state defines.","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"draft","label":"Draft","x":0,"y":0.5,"kind":"start"},{"id":"mod","label":"Moderation","x":1.25,"y":0.5},{"id":"pub","label":"Published","x":2.5,"y":0.5,"kind":"final"}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"draft","to":"mod","label":"publish()"},{"id":"e2","from":"mod","to":"pub","label":"approve()"},{"id":"e3","from":"mod","to":"draft","label":"reject()"}],"activeId":"draft","firedEdgeId":"$undefined","label":"document lifecycle"}},{"view":"state","codeLine":2,"narration":"Call publish() while in Draft: the Draft state handles it by moving the document to Moderation, it sets the next state itself.","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"draft","label":"Draft","x":0,"y":0.5,"kind":"start"},{"id":"mod","label":"Moderation","x":1.25,"y":0.5},{"id":"pub","label":"Published","x":2.5,"y":0.5,"kind":"final"}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"draft","to":"mod","label":"publish()"},{"id":"e2","from":"mod","to":"pub","label":"approve()"},{"id":"e3","from":"mod","to":"draft","label":"reject()"}],"activeId":"mod","firedEdgeId":"e1","label":"document lifecycle"},"vars":[["Draft.publish()","→ Moderation"]]},{"view":"state","narration":"Now in Moderation, the SAME publish()/approve() call behaves differently, an approval pushes it to Published. The object \"changed class\" without any if/else.","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"draft","label":"Draft","x":0,"y":0.5,"kind":"start"},{"id":"mod","label":"Moderation","x":1.25,"y":0.5},{"id":"pub","label":"Published","x":2.5,"y":0.5,"kind":"final"}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"draft","to":"mod","label":"publish()"},{"id":"e2","from":"mod","to":"pub","label":"approve()"},{"id":"e3","from":"mod","to":"draft","label":"reject()"}],"activeId":"pub","firedEdgeId":"e2","label":"document lifecycle"},"vars":[["Moderation.approve()","→ Published"]]},{"view":"state","narration":"Each state owns its behaviour and its exits. Adding a new state (say \"Archived\") is a new class, existing states are untouched. That's the State pattern: a state machine as objects.","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"draft","label":"Draft","x":0,"y":0.5,"kind":"start"},{"id":"mod","label":"Moderation","x":1.25,"y":0.5},{"id":"pub","label":"Published","x":2.5,"y":0.5,"kind":"final"}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"draft","to":"mod","label":"publish()"},{"id":"e2","from":"mod","to":"pub","label":"approve()"},{"id":"e3","from":"mod","to":"draft","label":"reject()"}],"activeId":"pub","firedEdgeId":"$undefined","label":"document lifecycle"},"vars":[["add a state","= add a class ✓"]]}]}]}}]]}]
